Drive OUT6 (J4 pin 6) to ground as soon as IN1 or IN3 is high.
Apply these three edits to TeslaBMSV2.ino (firmver 200206).

1) firmver:
- int firmver = 200205;
+ int firmver = 200206;

2) In setup(), after analogWriteFrequency(OUT8, pwmfreq):
+  analogWrite(OUT6, 0); // ISA unpowered until IN1 or IN3

   and change the OUT6 pinMode comment to:
   pinMode(OUT6, OUTPUT); // ISA enable (low-side, J4 pin 6)

3) At the very top of loop(), before while (Can0.available()):
+  // ISA enable: IN1 key or IN3 charge → OUT6 FET on (J4 pin 6 to GND)
+  {
+    bool keyOrCharge = (digitalRead(IN1) == HIGH) || (digitalRead(IN3) == HIGH);
+    isaInhibit = !keyOrCharge;
+    analogWrite(OUT6, keyOrCharge ? 255 : 0);
+  }
